# Common vs Libs vs Addons placement

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `Common/` | First-party shared source — **not** a standalone game AddOn |
| `Common/UI/` | First-party shared window and widget helpers (`WoWF.UI`) |
| `Libs/` | Third-party vendored packages — **filenames never renamed** on package |
| `Addons/<Name>/` | Addon root — TOC, `tkmm.config`, `RELEASE.md`, icons. Code is in `src/` |
| `Scripts/` | Dev tooling only |

## Addon startup

See rule `addon-main-startup`: every addon has `src/Main.lua` (VERSION + load banner). TOC order is `Common\...` → Libs (if needed) → `src\Main.lua` → feature scripts in `src\`. See rule `addon-src-folder`.

## Packaging (install / build / dev)

Shared helper: [`Scripts/wowf-vendor-common.sh`](Scripts/wowf-vendor-common.sh) (`vendor_shared`).

Copy the whole folder. Do not rename files or folders inside `Common/` or `Libs/`.

| Workspace | Packaged |
|-----|----|
| `Common/**` | `Common/**` beside `src/` |
| `Libs/**` | `Libs/**` |

```
Interface/AddOns/JunkMaster/
 Common/DevMode.lua
 Common/Logger.lua
 Common/UI/CircleIcon.lua
 Common/UI/Core.lua
 Common/UI/Window.lua
 Libs/LibStub/LibStub.lua
 Libs/LibEditMode/...
 src/Main.lua
 src/JunkMaster.lua
 JunkMaster.toc
```

`Common/` and `Libs/` are never installed as their own top-level AddOns. The packaged addon has `Common/` beside `src/`, and `Libs/` when the addon uses a library.

### Development mode

- Workspace `Common/DevMode.lua` sets `WoWF.DevMode = true`.
- **install / in-game via install|dev:** keep `DevMode = true`.
- **build (production Outputs/):** rewrite to `WoWF.DevMode = false`.
- Addons check `WoWF.DevMode` for extra logging / experimental behavior.

## TOC rules

- List Common files by their real path (`Common\DevMode.lua`, `Common\Logger.lua`, `Common\UI\Core.lua`).
- Vendored libs: list real `Libs\...` paths.
- Order: Common → Libs → `src\Main.lua` → feature scripts in `src\`. Load `Common\UI\Core.lua` before `Common\UI\Window.lua`.
- Do **not** list renamed names like `CommonDevMode.lua`, `CommonLogger.lua`, or `CommonUI\Core.lua`.
- Do **not** copy `Common/` or `Libs/` into workspace `Addons/<Name>/` by hand — install/build/dev does that.
- Do **not** use `require`/imports; WoW loads TOC entries in order into the addon environment.

## Placement

- Put logic in `Common/` when it can reasonably be shared across addons (first-party).
- Put window and widget helpers in `Common/UI/`.
- Put third-party libraries in `Libs/<PackageName>/`.
- Put code in `Addons/<Name>/src/` when it is specific to that addon’s TOC, slash commands, or feature surface. Leave the TOC, `tkmm.config`, `RELEASE.md`, and icons at the addon root.

## When unsure — ask

If placement is unclear, **ask before creating or moving it**. Prefer a short question with a recommendation, e.g.:

> This looks shareable (X). Put it in `Common/` or keep it under `Addons/JunkMaster`?

Use those answers to refine future placement without re-asking the same category once established in the conversation.
